/* ══════════ COUNCIL MEDIAN SALE PRICE ══════════

   Cotality "median sales price last 3 months" by council, one value a month
   from 1980-03, for the councils of Greater Adelaide and Greater Brisbane.
   The same measure and the same shape as the capital-city series inside the
   tool, so a property can be set against its own council on the same terms it
   is set against its capital.

   Houses and units are separate lines. A 0 is not a low month - it is a month
   with no figure, either because Cotality published none or because the
   quarter behind it held fewer than 30 sales, which is the same floor the
   capital-city series uses. Early Adelaide ran on a handful of sales a quarter
   and produced "medians" that meant nothing.

   Known holes, left as holes rather than filled:
     - every South Australian council is missing 2019-10; that month's
       workbook carries New South Wales localities where the SA rows belong
     - units in the smaller councils are sparse to absent - Playford, Scenic
       Rim, Lockyer Valley, Yankalilla, Walkerville and Somerset among them

   Built from corelogiclgadata_part_3..6.xlsx (to 2018-06) and the monthly
   Market Trends workbooks (from 2018-07). Council names are normalised onto
   the spelling suburb-lga.js uses: Cotality writes them plain outside
   2018-08..2023-06 and ABS-style within it, and where both spellings covered
   the same month the values agreed every time.
*/
